# Implementation Plan - Expanding Group Types & Group-Specific Fields

We are expanding the community group types in Komunity from the current 3-4 options (`bereavement`, `excess`, `emergency`, `custom`) to include 4 new dedicated group types:
1. **Churches & Religious Groups** (`church`)
2. **Stokvels & Savings Clubs** (`stokvel`)
3. **Student Bodies & Societies** (`student`)
4. **Sports Clubs & Teams** (`sports`)

To make each group type deeply functional and relevant, we are introducing **group-type specific configuration fields and features** across the backend models, REST API, web frontend, and mobile apps.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Data Model Design Choice**
> We propose introducing dedicated extension models linked to `Group` via `OneToOneField` (e.g. `GroupBereavementProfile`, `GroupChurchProfile`, `GroupStokvelProfile`, `GroupStudentProfile`, `GroupSportsProfile`). This keeps the core `Group` table clean while allowing type-specific validation, database constraints, and custom Django Admin forms.

> [!TIP]
> **Church Multiple Campaigns**
> For Church groups, we will enable church administrators to manage multiple simultaneous fund campaigns (e.g. Monthly Tithes, Building Fund, Missions, Special Offerings) linked directly to the church group wallet with campaign-level tracking and recurring contribution options.

